    "The purpose of the data collection was to address the following objectives [1] To investigate the use of oxygen optodes in quantifying sea ice primary production,  [2] To document changes in sea ice community productivity and algal taxonomic composition over the spring bloom and between high and low snow covers, and [3] To assess the dominant environmental factors driving variability in sea ice productivity."
